# Animation Patterns Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish patterns for implementing consistent, performant animations throughout the app. While specific animation styles may vary by context, the core principles should be followed.

## Best Practices
- Follow Material Design motion principles
- Implement animations that enhance usability, not distract
- Use implicit animations for simple state changes
- Use explicit animations for complex, coordinated animations
- Keep animations short (150-500ms) and purposeful
- Ensure animations work consistently across device capabilities
- Support animation disabling for accessibility
- Maintain consistent animation timings across similar interactions
- Implement proper entrance/exit animations for all elements
- Use staggered animations for related elements

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize animation-related components:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      animations/
        animation_constants.dart
        custom_animations.dart
        animation_controller_mixin.dart
        transitions/
          fade_scale_transition.dart
          slide_transition.dart
        curves/
          custom_curves.dart
    presentation/
      widgets/
        animated/
          animated_message_bubble.dart
          animated_list_item.dart
          animated_loading_indicator.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Define animation durations in a central constants file
- Use semantic naming for animations: `fadeInTransition`, `slideOutAnimation`
- Implement reusable animation widgets
- Use composition for complex animations
- Extract animation logic into dedicated classes/mixins
- Implement proper disposal of animation controllers
- Document animation parameters and behaviors
- Use consistent curve types for similar animations

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Limit animations during critical user interactions
- Use repaint boundaries to isolate frequently animating widgets
- Avoid animating properties that trigger layout (prefer opacity, transform)
- Profile animations with Flutter DevTools
- Implement frame throttling for low-end devices
- Reduce or disable animations based on device capabilities
- Use hardware acceleration when appropriate
- Batch animations that occur simultaneously
- Implement lazy rendering for animated lists
- Cache pre-computed animation values when possible

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test animations on low-end devices
- Verify animations respect reduced motion settings
- Test animation performance with Flutter performance overlay
- Validate proper animation controller disposal
- Test animations with different screen sizes and orientations
- Verify animations complete properly when interrupted
- Ensure animations don't interfere with user interactions
- Test animations with different frame rates
- Implement visual regression tests for critical animations
- Benchmark complex animations for performance impact